
Note: This file can be accessed under the CLI by typing (or printing)
	'THISSALA.HELP'

BUGS FIXED / FEATURES ADDED IN REVISION 0.60

1)  New puzzles, new objects, new commands

2)  LOOK IN or LOOK INTO has been implemented

3)  Revision 0.60 has been rehosted to AOS/VS.  The THISSALA macro
    will automatically start up the correct game

4)  The monster are again wondering the different sections.  They
    will attack, but with no strength as of now.  There was a bug
    reported that I believe is now fixed.  This should prove or dis-
    prove this.

BUGS FIXED / FEATURES ADDED IN REVISION 0.55
============================================

1)  Some early developed puzzles have been completed, and some
    early objects have had their attributes brought up to date

2)  The RECALL command has been greatly modified and should now
    work correctly (Note that old games will not recall across
    new revisions

3)  The monsters have been moved away until a decision has been reached
    concerning how to handle POWER and COOR.


BUGS FIXED / FEATURES ADDED IN REVISION 0.54
============================================

1)  THISSALA now supports non-ansi and non-screenedit terminals.  If
    the terminal read fails using screenedit I/O, THISSALA will retry
    the I/O using a standard read

2)  THISSALA now has this help file to help you with


COMMAND SUMMARY
===============

THISSALA  briefly describe the game

BRIEF     normal mode
BUG       submit a bug report (see RECOMMEND) (B is a valid abbr)
CLI       proc up a CLI son process and block
INVENT    report player's objects  (I and INV are valid abbreviations)
LOOK <IN> return expanded room descriptor or describe the interior of
          an object  (L is a valid abbreviation)
RTOD      return the real time of day
SCORE     report score    (SC is a valid abbreviation)
TIME      return the internal game time of day (TI is a valid abbr.)
VERBOSE   alway return full room descriptor

STATUS    return current player information
-------------------------------------------

	STATUS<NL>

	Power:     xxxx
	Coor:	   xxxx
	Magic:     xxxx
	Wisdom:    xxxx
	Knowledge: xxxx

LOG	  turn on/off logging
-----------------------------

	LOG<NL>
	Filename: <logfile_name>

	 or

	LOG<NL>

RECOMMEND recommend a sentence or word for addition to vocab 
------------------------------------------------------------
          (R is a valid abbreviation).  The easiest way to use this
          is upon typing a sentence which contains an unknown word,
          type ^A (recover the sentence), ^H (position to beginning)
          ^E (insert) R<space> ^E (end insert) <NL>.  This will enter
          the entire sentence into the recommendations file.  Thanks.

SAVE      save a game
---------------------

	SAVE<NL>
	Filename: <game_name>
	Game saved

RECALL    recall a game
-----------------------

	RECALL<NL>
	Filename: <game_name>
	Game recalled
 

Collectives
-----------

The constructions ALL / EVERYTHING / BUT / EXCEPT work for the TAKE and
DROP commands (and their synonyms), as does multiple objects, allowing 
constructs like:
 
TAKE EVERYTHING EXCEPT THE BILL AND THE SHOVEL.
 
            and

PICK UP ALL BUT THE BIRD

